# The `wifi` producer: the Wi-Fi userland facts, as two disjoint packages.
#
# Plain `KEY=value` lines only: no logic, no command substitution, no
# expansion. Safe to source from bash and to parse with grep/sed from anything
# else, and checked for that shape by build-env/deb/build.sh before it is
# sourced. build-env/deb/README.md documents every field.

# Two packages, one producer. They are separate because a board chooses Wi-Fi
# client and access point INDEPENDENTLY: a combined package would make a
# station-only board install hostapd. Bluetooth is its own producer
# (rootfs/packages-src/bluetooth) for the same reason at the producer
# level -- selecting, declining and rebuilding one radio must not touch the
# other. No path and no relationship is shared between any of them.
PACKAGES="mos-wifi mos-wifi-ap"

# `all` and not `amd64 arm64`. Every payload here is a systemd unit or a
# symlink, with no ELF anywhere, so one archive is correct for every image this
# repository builds.
ARCHES="all"

# `family` is rootfs/packages-src itself, and it is here for one file: the
# shared copyright. The primary build context is this producer's OWN
# directory, so anything held in common with the sibling producers sits one
# level up and has to be named to be reachable.
#
# The unit bodies are copied BYTE-IDENTICAL out of the tree that ships them,
# so that packaging them cannot become a second, drifting rendering of the
# same files. They live under boards/cx3576 because that is where they were
# first written; their content is a radio-application fact, not a board fact
# -- the board facts they are paired with (the radio kernel modules, the
# firmware) stay in mos-board-cx3576.
BUILD_CONTEXTS="family=rootfs/packages-src radio-units=boards/cx3576/overlay/etc/systemd/system"

# Neither package enables a unit at multi-user.target: each ships a
# local-fs.target.wants link instead, which this field does not count, so both
# write the zero rather than leaving a reader to infer it from a payload that
# does contain enablement links.
ENABLEMENT="mos-wifi=0 mos-wifi-ap=0"
